Subject: [PATCH] Reconcile the additional r9s domains with One UI 9 security boundaries

The newer API30 vendor adds dmd, hal_kg30_default and the MLS-trusted
vendor_telephony_silentlogging_app. Extend only the reviewed legacy
grant restrictions to those actual additional domains. Keep unrelated
permissions, aliases, and every donor allow/neverallow byte-for-byte.
Remove the vendor application's forbidden modem-logging service lookup;
do not exempt it from either the current or old public assertion.

The donor domain.te:607 already permits dmd and hal_kg30_default to
execute shell_exec/toolbox_exec through base_typeattr_412. Reconcile
only those exact source/target/permission intersections in the obsolete
API30 guards; retain their guards against every other executable.
No allow absent from the original complete policy is introduced.

